{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-156418-r4518639","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Lentil, Potato, and Tomato Curry","sourcePageId":156418,"sourceRevision":"4518639","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T16:31:22Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Lentil%2C%20Potato%2C%20and%20Tomato%20Curry&oldid=4518639","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:08:14.377Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Indian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for curry","Category:Recipes for stew","Category:Recipes using bay leaf","Category:Recipes using cayenne","Category:Recipes using garam masala","Category:Recipes using honey","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes using potato","Category:Recipes using red lentil","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes using tomato","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Vegetarian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"7183e2c0902ff9e078eb3988f087218671ec3292228c5555c583ee824d7d848a","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Stew recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\nThis creates a healthy, inexpensive and easy stew with depths of flavor. This recipe is fairly low on the heat scale, but feel free to add more cayenne pepper to up its spiciness. It is excellent served with chapatis or rice.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Lentil|red split lentils]]\n* 4 cups water\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaf]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]] or [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Olive Oil|olive oil]]\n* 2 large [[Cookbook:Potato|potatoes]], cut into ½ inch [[Cookbook:Cube|cubes]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:turmeric|turmeric]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]]\n* 28 [[Cookbook:Ounce|ounces]] canned diced [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]]\n* 2 teaspoons [[Cookbook:garam masala|garam masala]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Honey|honey]] or [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n==Procedure==\n# In a large pot, combine and cook water, lentils, salt and bay leaf. \n# In a large [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|frying pan]], combine potatoes, turmeric, cayenne pepper, olive oil and margarine. [[Cookbook:Frying|Fry]] for 5–10 minutes. \n# Add potato mixture to the pot with the lentils along with all remaining ingredients. Cook until the potatoes are soft and tender.\n# Remove bay leaf before serving.\n[[Category:Recipes using potato]]\n[[Category:Recipes using red lentil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tomato]]\n[[Category:Recipes for curry]]\n[[Category:Recipes for stew]]\n[[Category:Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bay leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garam masala]]\n[[Category:Recipes using honey]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Lentil, Potato, and Tomato Curry","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 cup red split lentils","sourceText":"1 